      <title>Developing nations face triple shock from energy crisis, El Niño and borrowing costs, UN warns</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/11/developing-nations-triple-shock-energy-crisis-el-nino-borrowing-costs-un-warns</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;UN’s development arm calls for urgent action as crises could ‘throw tens if not hundreds of millions back into poverty’&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Developing countries face a triple shock from the energy crisis, El Niño and surging borrowing costs and need urgent support from the international community, the UN’s development arm has warned.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Speaking before the International Monetary Fund (IMF) and World Bank annual meetings in Bangkok this week,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;the UNDP’s administrator, Alexander De Croo, called for “solidarity and global action”.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/11/developing-nations-triple-shock-energy-crisis-el-nino-borrowing-costs-un-warns"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
